  "details": "PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language commonly used with the Apache HTTP Server.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * php: php: Out-of-bounds read via empty HTTP redirect Location header (CVE-2026-93682)\n  * php: PHP: Archive entry injection via integer overflow in TAR parser (CVE-2026-6103)\n  * php: PHP: Denial of Service via heap buffer overflow in SOAP client (CVE-2025-14181)\n  * php: php: Denial of Service via unbounded recursion in SOAP parser (CVE-2026-91765)\n  * php: php: Credential disclosure via cross-origin HTTP redirects (CVE-2026-91766)\n  * php: php: Information disclosure via crafted TLS server certificate (CVE-2026-91767)\n  * php: php: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read in mysqlnd wire protocol parser (CVE-2025-1218)\n  * php: php: Access control bypass via partial IPv6 address comparison (CVE-2026-91768)\n  * php: php: Information disclosure via out-of-bounds read in stream filters (CVE-2026-92842)\n  * php: php: Server impersonation via Common Name fallback in TLS verification (CVE-2026-91769)\n  * php: OOM bailout during request parsing leads to memory corruption and RCE (CVE-2026-109618)\n  * php: fatal error handling retains stale request state leading to use-after-free (CVE-2026-109619)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
